  "final_message": "I have initiated a scan of the project structure and am waiting for the command to finish.\nI am checking all occurrences of `channel` across the codebase.\nI am listing the test files to check references.\nI am waiting for the file listing to complete.\nI am checking the root directory files.\nI am checking the git commit history to see previous deprecations and event changes.\nRemoving `channel` directly from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is not permitted under the repository's architectural rules defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be removed directly\n1. **Downstream Breakage**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is a public contract consumed by external services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing the `channel` property from the v3 schema is a non-additive, breaking change.\n2. **Order Model Dependency**: If `channel` were removed from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) and [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38) models, [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) could no longer supply `channel` to deployed consumers expecting it.\n\n### Recommended Deprecation Path\nTo deprecate `channel` in compliance with **ARCH-4**:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) (and optionally in [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29)/[`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38)).\n2. If callers should no longer be required to provide it, introduce a schema evolution (such as a new schema version or making the field optional with a default/fallback) while coordinating with the `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` teams.\n3. Remove the field only after all consumers have migrated away.\n",
